{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777417081,"nonce":"7Y4v5r2lCG34vZPug45/LIXGQE0=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAxZiQg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/101","origin":"github"},"title":"Add sound_speed_bridge launch to bizzyboat core (AML SVS on gabby ttyS1 → M3 via UDP)","message":"## Summary\n\nAdd a `sound_speed_launch.py` subsystem launch to `bizzyboat_project11` and wire it into `core_launch.py` so the new `sound_speed_bridge` driver runs as part of the standard boat bringup.\n\nThis is the boat-specific configuration layer for the generic driver added in [rolker/marine_tools#4](https://github.com/rolker/marine_tools/pull/4) — wires up the AML SVS on gabby's `/dev/ttyS1`, points the Valeport-format UDP fan-out at `mercat:20003` (M3's built-in Valeport listener), and uses the existing `frame_prefix` substitution so the published topic's `frame_id` is `bizzy/sound_speed_sensor`.\n\n## Files affected\n\n- `bizzyboat_project11/launch/sound_speed_launch.py` (new) — subsystem launch with bizzyboat-specific defaults.\n- `bizzyboat_project11/launch/core_launch.py` — `IncludeLaunchDescription` inside the existing `GroupAction` (so it inherits namespace + frame_prefix).\n- `bizzyboat_project11/package.xml` — add `\u003cexec_depend\u003esound_speed_bridge\u003c/exec_depend\u003e`.\n\n## Defaults (overridable via launch arguments)\n\n| Parameter | Default | Notes |\n|-----------|---------|-------|\n| `device` | `/dev/ttyS1` | gabby's COM2 — AML SVS confirmed connected here 2026-04-28 |\n| `baud` | `9600` | |\n| `parser` | `aml` | |\n| `frame_id` | `\u003cframe_prefix\u003esound_speed_sensor` | typically `bizzy/sound_speed_sensor` |\n| `udp_hosts` | `['mercat']` | M3 host on the boat LAN |\n| `udp_ports` | `[20003]` | M3's Valeport UDP listener |\n| `udp_formats` | `['valeport']` | byte-exact replacement for the PowerShell stand-in |\n\n## Dependency\n\nHard dependency on [rolker/marine_tools#4](https://github.com/rolker/marine_tools/pull/4) — the `sound_speed_bridge` package must be available for this launch to actually start. This PR can be opened and reviewed in parallel but should be merged after #4 to avoid a broken bringup on the default branch.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] `colcon build --packages-select bizzyboat_project11` succeeds\n- [ ] `ros2 launch bizzyboat_project11 sound_speed_launch.py` brings up `sound_speed_bridge` standalone\n- [ ] Smoke test on gabby against the live AML SVS: ROS topic `/bizzy/sound_speed` publishes at ~26 Hz with valid m/s values; M3 receives Valeport UDP and shows live SV; `/diagnostics` carries `sound_speed_m_s` value with `OK` status\n- [ ] Run via full `core_launch.py` to confirm namespace and frame_prefix wiring\n- [ ] PowerShell stand-in `aml_bridge.ps1` on mercat confirmed obsolete after smoke test (separate cleanup)\n\n## Related\n\n- Depends on [rolker/marine_tools#4](https://github.com/rolker/marine_tools/pull/4)\n- Replaces interim `aml_bridge.ps1` PowerShell script on mercat (memory: `project_aml_bridge_powershell.md`)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}